msgid "Part 3 — Working with Paths"
msgstr "Partie 3 — Travailler avec les chemins"

msgid ""
"Every key of a nested dictionary is reached by a path, the list of keys "
"from the top level down to it. This part lists these paths, moves along "
"them, filters them, writes them in a compact form, and uses that form to "
"check a dictionary against a list of what it should contain. How paths "
"are defined is explained in :doc:`/concepts/paths`, "
":doc:`/concepts/compact_paths` and :doc:`/concepts/coverage`."
msgstr ""
"Chaque clé d’un dictionnaire imbriqué est atteinte par un chemin, la "
"liste des clés qui mène du premier niveau jusqu’à elle. Cette partie "
"énumère ces chemins, se déplace le long de ceux-ci, les filtre, les écrit"
" sous une forme compacte, et utilise cette forme pour vérifier un "
"dictionnaire par rapport à une liste de ce qu’il doit contenir. La "
"définition des chemins est expliquée dans :doc:`/concepts/paths`, "
":doc:`/concepts/compact_paths` et :doc:`/concepts/coverage`."

msgid "The examples use the first floor of the house:"
msgstr "Les exemples utilisent le premier étage de la maison :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> first_floor = NestedDictionary({\n"
"...     \"bedroom\": {\"lights\": \"ceiling\", \"heating\": {\"type\": "
"\"radiator\", \"power\": 1000}},\n"
"...     \"bathroom\": {\"lights\": \"mirror\", \"heating\": {\"type\": "
"\"towel rail\"}},\n"
"... })"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> first_floor = NestedDictionary({\n"
"...     \"bedroom\": {\"lights\": \"ceiling\", \"heating\": {\"type\": "
"\"radiator\", \"power\": 1000}},\n"
"...     \"bathroom\": {\"lights\": \"mirror\", \"heating\": {\"type\": "
"\"towel rail\"}},\n"
"... })"

msgid "Listing the paths"
msgstr "Énumérer les chemins"

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.paths` returns a "
":class:`~ndict_tools.PathsView`. It plays for paths the role that "
":meth:`dict.keys` plays for keys: it holds one path per key, at every "
"level, in the order of the keys."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.paths` renvoie un "
":class:`~ndict_tools.PathsView`. Il joue pour les chemins le rôle que "
":meth:`dict.keys` joue pour les clés : il contient un chemin par clé, à "
"tous les niveaux, dans l’ordre des clés."

msgid ""
">>> paths = first_floor.paths()\n"
">>> for path in paths:\n"
"...     print(path)\n"
"['bedroom']\n"
"['bedroom', 'lights']\n"
"['bedroom', 'heating']\n"
"['bedroom', 'heating', 'type']\n"
"['bedroom', 'heating', 'power']\n"
"['bathroom']\n"
"['bathroom', 'lights']\n"
"['bathroom', 'heating']\n"
"['bathroom', 'heating', 'type']"
msgstr ""
">>> paths = first_floor.paths()\n"
">>> for path in paths:\n"
"...     print(path)\n"
"['bedroom']\n"
"['bedroom', 'lights']\n"
"['bedroom', 'heating']\n"
"['bedroom', 'heating', 'type']\n"
"['bedroom', 'heating', 'power']\n"
"['bathroom']\n"
"['bathroom', 'lights']\n"
"['bathroom', 'heating']\n"
"['bathroom', 'heating', 'type']"

msgid "There are as many paths as keys, and ``in`` tests whether a path exists:"
msgstr ""
"Il y a autant de chemins que de clés, et ``in`` teste si un chemin existe"
" :"

msgid ""
">>> len(paths)\n"
"9\n"
">>> [\"bathroom\", \"heating\"] in paths\n"
"True\n"
">>> [\"bathroom\", \"heating\", \"power\"] in paths\n"
"False"
msgstr ""
">>> len(paths)\n"
"9\n"
">>> [\"bathroom\", \"heating\"] in paths\n"
"True\n"
">>> [\"bathroom\", \"heating\", \"power\"] in paths\n"
"False"

msgid ""
"Unlike :meth:`dict.keys`, the view does not follow later changes. It "
"reads the dictionary the first time it is used and keeps that state. To "
"see the paths of a dictionary after a change, call "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.paths` again:"
msgstr ""
"Contrairement à :meth:`dict.keys`, la vue ne suit pas les modifications "
"ultérieures. Elle lit le dictionnaire lors de sa première utilisation et "
"conserve cet état. Pour voir les chemins d’un dictionnaire après une "
"modification, appelez de nouveau "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.paths` :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> first_floor[\"office\"] = {\"lights\": \"desk lamp\"}\n"
">>> len(paths)\n"
"9\n"
">>> len(first_floor.paths())\n"
"11\n"
">>> del first_floor[\"office\"]"
msgstr ""
">>> first_floor[\"office\"] = {\"lights\": \"desk lamp\"}\n"
">>> len(paths)\n"
"9\n"
">>> len(first_floor.paths())\n"
"11\n"
">>> del first_floor[\"office\"]"

msgid "Moving along the paths"
msgstr "Se déplacer le long des chemins"

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.PathsView.get_children` returns the keys just below a"
" path, and :meth:`~ndict_tools.PathsView.has_children` whether there are "
"any:"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.PathsView.get_children` renvoie les clés situées "
"juste sous un chemin, et :meth:`~ndict_tools.PathsView.has_children` "
"indique s’il y en a :"

msgid ""
">>> paths = first_floor.paths()\n"
">>> paths.get_children([\"bedroom\"])\n"
"['lights', 'heating']\n"
">>> paths.get_children([\"bedroom\", \"lights\"])\n"
"[]\n"
">>> paths.has_children([\"bedroom\", \"heating\"])\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> paths = first_floor.paths()\n"
">>> paths.get_children([\"bedroom\"])\n"
"['lights', 'heating']\n"
">>> paths.get_children([\"bedroom\", \"lights\"])\n"
"[]\n"
">>> paths.has_children([\"bedroom\", \"heating\"])\n"
"True"

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.PathsView.get_subtree_paths` returns a path and every"
" path below it, :meth:`~ndict_tools.PathsView.get_leaf_paths` the paths "
"of the keys without children:"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.PathsView.get_subtree_paths` renvoie un chemin et "
"tous les chemins situés en dessous, "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.PathsView.get_leaf_paths` les chemins des clés sans "
"enfant :"

msgid ""
">>> paths.get_subtree_paths([\"bedroom\", \"heating\"])\n"
"[['bedroom', 'heating'], ['bedroom', 'heating', 'type'], ['bedroom', "
"'heating', 'power']]\n"
">>> paths.get_leaf_paths()\n"
"[['bedroom', 'lights'], ['bedroom', 'heating', 'type'], ['bedroom', "
"'heating', 'power'], ['bathroom', 'lights'], ['bathroom', 'heating', "
"'type']]"
msgstr ""
">>> paths.get_subtree_paths([\"bedroom\", \"heating\"])\n"
"[['bedroom', 'heating'], ['bedroom', 'heating', 'type'], ['bedroom', "
"'heating', 'power']]\n"
">>> paths.get_leaf_paths()\n"
"[['bedroom', 'lights'], ['bedroom', 'heating', 'type'], ['bedroom', "
"'heating', 'power'], ['bathroom', 'lights'], ['bathroom', 'heating', "
"'type']]"

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.PathsView.get_depth` returns the number of levels, "
"like :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.height`: the room, the "
"equipment and its settings."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.PathsView.get_depth` renvoie le nombre de niveaux, "
"comme :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.height` : la pièce, "
"l’équipement et ses réglages."

msgid ""
">>> paths.get_depth()\n"
"3"
msgstr ""
">>> paths.get_depth()\n"
"3"

msgid "Filtering paths"
msgstr "Filtrer les chemins"

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.PathsView.filter_paths` keeps the paths for which a "
"function returns ``True``. The function receives each path as a list. "
"Where is the type of heating recorded, and which keys sit three levels "
"down?"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.PathsView.filter_paths` garde les chemins pour "
"lesquels une fonction renvoie ``True``. La fonction reçoit chaque chemin "
"sous forme de liste. Où le type de chauffage est-il enregistré, et "
"quelles clés se trouvent trois niveaux plus bas ?"

msgid ""
">>> paths.filter_paths(lambda path: path[-1] == \"type\")\n"
"[['bedroom', 'heating', 'type'], ['bathroom', 'heating', 'type']]\n"
">>> paths.filter_paths(lambda path: len(path) == 3)\n"
"[['bedroom', 'heating', 'type'], ['bedroom', 'heating', 'power'], "
"['bathroom', 'heating', 'type']]"
msgstr ""
">>> paths.filter_paths(lambda path: path[-1] == \"type\")\n"
"[['bedroom', 'heating', 'type'], ['bathroom', 'heating', 'type']]\n"
">>> paths.filter_paths(lambda path: len(path) == 3)\n"
"[['bedroom', 'heating', 'type'], ['bedroom', 'heating', 'power'], "
"['bathroom', 'heating', 'type']]"

msgid "Compact paths"
msgstr "Chemins compacts"

msgid ""
"The list of paths repeats every prefix: ``bedroom`` appears in five "
"paths. :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.compact_paths` returns a "
":class:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView`, which writes each key once. Its "
":attr:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.structure` is a list with one entry "
"per top-level key: the key, then its children; a child that has children "
"of its own is a list in turn."
msgstr ""
"La liste des chemins répète chaque préfixe : ``bedroom`` apparaît dans "
"cinq chemins. :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.compact_paths` renvoie"
" un :class:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView`, qui écrit chaque clé une "
"seule fois. Son attribut :attr:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.structure` "
"est une liste avec une entrée par clé de premier niveau : la clé, puis "
"ses enfants ; un enfant qui a lui-même des enfants est à son tour une "
"liste."

msgid ""
">>> compact = first_floor.compact_paths()\n"
">>> compact.structure\n"
"[['bedroom', 'lights', ['heating', 'type', 'power']], ['bathroom', "
"'lights', ['heating', 'type']]]"
msgstr ""
">>> compact = first_floor.compact_paths()\n"
">>> compact.structure\n"
"[['bedroom', 'lights', ['heating', 'type', 'power']], ['bathroom', "
"'lights', ['heating', 'type']]]"

msgid ""
"The compact view holds the same paths as the other one, and offers the "
"same methods. :meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.expand` writes them in"
" full, and the two views convert into each other:"
msgstr ""
"La vue compacte contient les mêmes chemins que l’autre et offre les mêmes"
" méthodes. :meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.expand` les écrit en "
"entier, et les deux vues se convertissent l’une en l’autre :"

msgid ""
">>> compact.expand() == list(paths)\n"
"True\n"
">>> type(compact.to_paths()).__name__\n"
"'PathsView'\n"
">>> type(paths.to_compact()).__name__\n"
"'CompactPathsView'"
msgstr ""
">>> compact.expand() == list(paths)\n"
"True\n"
">>> type(compact.to_paths()).__name__\n"
"'PathsView'\n"
">>> type(paths.to_compact()).__name__\n"
"'CompactPathsView'"

msgid "Checking a dictionary against a list"
msgstr "Vérifier un dictionnaire par rapport à une liste"

msgid ""
"A compact view can serve as a checklist. When you take over a house, you "
"check, room by room, the lights and the type of heating. The checklist is"
" built from a dictionary whose keys are the items to check; its values do"
" not matter:"
msgstr ""
"Une vue compacte peut servir de liste de contrôle. Lorsque vous reprenez "
"une maison, vous vérifiez, pièce par pièce, l’éclairage et le type de "
"chauffage. La liste de contrôle est construite à partir d’un dictionnaire"
" dont les clés sont les points à vérifier ; ses valeurs n’ont pas "
"d’importance :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> checklist = NestedDictionary({\n"
"...     \"bedroom\": {\"lights\": None, \"heating\": {\"type\": None}},\n"
"...     \"bathroom\": {\"lights\": None, \"heating\": {\"type\": None}},\n"
"... }).compact_paths()"
msgstr ""
">>> checklist = NestedDictionary({\n"
"...     \"bedroom\": {\"lights\": None, \"heating\": {\"type\": None}},\n"
"...     \"bathroom\": {\"lights\": None, \"heating\": {\"type\": None}},\n"
"... }).compact_paths()"

msgid ""
"Four methods compare the paths of the checklist with those of a "
"dictionary. Two of them list the differences:"
msgstr ""
"Quatre méthodes comparent les chemins de la liste de contrôle à ceux d’un"
" dictionnaire. Deux d’entre elles énumèrent les différences :"

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.missing_paths` lists the paths of "
"the checklist that the dictionary does not have: what is missing from the"
" house;"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.missing_paths` énumère les chemins "
"de la liste de contrôle que le dictionnaire n’a pas : ce qui manque à la "
"maison ;"

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.uncovered_paths` lists the paths of "
"the dictionary that the checklist does not have: what the house has "
"beyond the list."
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.uncovered_paths` énumère les chemins"
" du dictionnaire que la liste de contrôle n’a pas : ce que la maison a en"
" plus de la liste."

msgid ""
"The first floor has everything on the list, and also the power of the "
"bedroom radiator, which the list does not mention:"
msgstr ""
"Le premier étage a tout ce qui figure sur la liste, et aussi la puissance"
" du radiateur de la chambre, que la liste ne mentionne pas :"

msgid ""
">>> checklist.missing_paths(first_floor)\n"
"[]\n"
">>> checklist.uncovered_paths(first_floor)\n"
"[['bedroom', 'heating', 'power']]"
msgstr ""
">>> checklist.missing_paths(first_floor)\n"
"[]\n"
">>> checklist.uncovered_paths(first_floor)\n"
"[['bedroom', 'heating', 'power']]"

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.coverage` is the share of the "
"dictionary's paths that the checklist describes: here 8 of 9. "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.is_covering` is ``True`` only when "
"the two sets of paths are the same:"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.coverage` est la part des chemins du"
" dictionnaire que la liste de contrôle décrit : ici 8 sur 9. "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.CompactPathsView.is_covering` ne vaut ``True`` que "
"lorsque les deux ensembles de chemins sont identiques :"

msgid ""
">>> round(checklist.coverage(first_floor), 2)\n"
"0.89\n"
">>> checklist.is_covering(first_floor)\n"
"False"
msgstr ""
">>> round(checklist.coverage(first_floor), 2)\n"
"0.89\n"
">>> checklist.is_covering(first_floor)\n"
"False"

msgid ""
"Coverage looks at the dictionary only. In a bathroom without lights, "
"every path of the house is on the list, so coverage is complete, although"
" an item of the list is missing. Only ``missing_paths`` reports it:"
msgstr ""
"La couverture ne regarde que le dictionnaire. Dans une salle de bains "
"sans éclairage, chaque chemin de la maison figure sur la liste ; la "
"couverture est donc complète, bien qu’un point de la liste manque. Seule "
"``missing_paths`` le signale :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> unlit = NestedDictionary({\n"
"...     \"bedroom\": {\"lights\": \"ceiling\", \"heating\": {\"type\": "
"\"radiator\"}},\n"
"...     \"bathroom\": {\"heating\": {\"type\": \"towel rail\"}},\n"
"... })\n"
">>> checklist.coverage(unlit)\n"
"1.0\n"
">>> checklist.missing_paths(unlit)\n"
"[['bathroom', 'lights']]\n"
">>> checklist.is_covering(unlit)\n"
"False"
msgstr ""
">>> unlit = NestedDictionary({\n"
"...     \"bedroom\": {\"lights\": \"ceiling\", \"heating\": {\"type\": "
"\"radiator\"}},\n"
"...     \"bathroom\": {\"heating\": {\"type\": \"towel rail\"}},\n"
"... })\n"
">>> checklist.coverage(unlit)\n"
"1.0\n"
">>> checklist.missing_paths(unlit)\n"
"[['bathroom', 'lights']]\n"
">>> checklist.is_covering(unlit)\n"
"False"

msgid ""
"To check that nothing on the list is missing, test ``missing_paths``. To "
"check that the house matches the list exactly, use ``is_covering``:"
msgstr ""
"Pour vérifier que rien ne manque sur la liste, testez ``missing_paths``. "
"Pour vérifier que la maison correspond exactement à la liste, utilisez "
"``is_covering`` :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> inspected = NestedDictionary({\n"
"...     \"bedroom\": {\"lights\": \"ceiling\", \"heating\": {\"type\": "
"\"radiator\"}},\n"
"...     \"bathroom\": {\"lights\": \"mirror\", \"heating\": {\"type\": "
"\"towel rail\"}},\n"
"... })\n"
">>> checklist.is_covering(inspected)\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> inspected = NestedDictionary({\n"
"...     \"bedroom\": {\"lights\": \"ceiling\", \"heating\": {\"type\": "
"\"radiator\"}},\n"
"...     \"bathroom\": {\"lights\": \"mirror\", \"heating\": {\"type\": "
"\"towel rail\"}},\n"
"... })\n"
">>> checklist.is_covering(inspected)\n"
"True"

